<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Boyd Dunlop</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1840">1840</a>–<a href="/years/1921">1921</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John Boyd Dunlop was a Scottish-born veterinary surgeon in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belfast">Belfast</a> who in 1888 developed a practical pneumatic tyre, first for his son's tricycle. Its rapid adoption for bicycles and then motor cars created a huge world demand for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rubber">rubber</a>, which drove the brutal exploitation of wild rubber in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congo-free-state">Congo Free State</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amazon">Amazon</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-boyd-dunlop.jpg" alt="John Boyd Dunlop" width="320" height="395" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:John_Boyd_Dunlop.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
